            <ArticleTitle>Electronic perturbation of supramolecular conjugates of porphyrins and phthalocyanines.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>2230-2232</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1039/c6cc09590a</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The redox potential of a supramolecular porphyrin-phthalocyanine heterodimer was perturbed by the stacking of an extra metalloporphyrin to the phthalocyanine. This stacking gave rise to π-π and electrostatic interactions between the tetracationic dimer and the tetraanionic metalloporphyrin, with a Au(iii) metalloporphyrin exhibiting a larger effect than Cu(ii) and Pd(ii) complexes among square planar complexes.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
